From: William Macready <william.macready@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:28:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] wip(f32-flip-slice2): S2a StructuralTest pins the new
 default

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 leanncd/test/DSL/Pipeline/StructuralTest.lean | 13 +++++++++++--
 papers/f32_flip_slice2_log.md                 |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/leanncd/test/DSL/Pipeline/StructuralTest.lean b/leanncd/test/DSL/Pipeline/StructuralTest.lean
index e8c18a6..d66eb49 100644
--- a/leanncd/test/DSL/Pipeline/StructuralTest.lean
+++ b/leanncd/test/DSL/Pipeline/StructuralTest.lean
@@ -167,10 +167,19 @@ run_cmd do
   | .ok (.ok .float32) => pure ()
   | .ok r => throwError s!"f32-plus-predicate graph: expected .ok .float32, got {repr r}"
 
--- (b) the same graph in the untyped (f64) spelling selects `.float64`.
+-- (b) the same graph in the untyped spelling selects `.float32`: plain `tensor` is the binary32
+--     default (the f32 default flip), so it agrees with the f32 spelling in (a).
 run_cmd do
   match storageOf [.tensor "Y" [axS], .tensor "X" [axS], .predicate "P" [axS]] "Y" ["X", "P"] with
   | .error m => throwError m
+  | .ok (.ok .float32) => pure ()
+  | .ok r => throwError s!"untyped-plus-predicate graph: expected .ok .float32, got {repr r}"
+
+-- (b') the same graph with the EXPLICIT binary64 spelling selects `.float64`.
+run_cmd do
+  match storageOf [.typedTensor .f64 "Y" [axS], .typedTensor .f64 "X" [axS], .predicate "P" [axS]]
+      "Y" ["X", "P"] with
+  | .error m => throwError m
   | .ok (.ok .float64) => pure ()
   | .ok r => throwError s!"f64-plus-predicate graph: expected .ok .float64, got {repr r}"
 
@@ -188,7 +197,7 @@ run_cmd do
 --     deliberately ordered `C`, `B`, `A`).
 run_cmd do
   match storageOf
-      [ .tensor "C" [axS], .tensor "B" [axS], .typedTensor .f32 "A" [axS]
+      [ .typedTensor .f64 "C" [axS], .typedTensor .f64 "B" [axS], .typedTensor .f32 "A" [axS]
       , .typedTensor .f32 "D" [axS] ]
       "D" ["A", "B", "C"] with
   | .error m => throwError m
diff --git a/papers/f32_flip_slice2_log.md b/papers/f32_flip_slice2_log.md
index 1e78357..994b259 100644
--- a/papers/f32_flip_slice2_log.md
+++ b/papers/f32_flip_slice2_log.md
@@ -1,3 +1,6 @@
 # f32 flip slice 2 prototype log
 
 - S1: applied the 4 one-line flips (Ast storageConstraintOfDecl tensor/linear + storageConstraintOfName? undeclared, Signature dtypeOfDecl tensor/linear/none, Compile.lean line 1410 stateSigs fallback) plus the old-default docstrings/comment. CLAIMED only, targeted build of LeanNCD pending (next entry).
+- S1 VERIFIED: targeted `lake build LeanNCD` with the flip: "Build completed successfully (8546 jobs)".
+- S2a (StructuralTest): CLAIMED edit only (b: untyped -> .float32, new b': explicit f64 -> .float64, d: B/C spelled f64); build pending.
+- S2b (ComplexElementTypeTest): CLAIMED edit only (new `neighbour` helper declares undeclared A/B/Y f64 explicitly; docs); build pending.
